{{also|Plankton}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|de|Plankton}}, {{coin|en|Victor Hensen|nat=German|occ=zoologist and marine biologist|nocat=1|nocap=1}} and derived from {{der|en|grc|πλαγκτός||[[drifter#English|drifter]]}}, from {{m|grc|πλάζω||I turn aside, wander}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈplæŋk.tən/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-plankton.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-plankton.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s|plankton}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[organism|Organism]]s, especially small and microscopic ones, that [[drift#Verb|drift]] in water.
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[plankter]], any single organism that drifts in water.

